config KERNEL_SIGNAL
    bool "Enable Signal"
    default n if KERNEL_RAM_PRESET_TINY || KERNEL_RAM_PRESET_SMALL
    default y
    depends on KERNEL_EXTKERNEL && ARCH_ARM_CORTEX_M
    depends on !BOX
    help
      Select y to build LiteOS with signal.

      Mutually exclusive with BOX. The signal-context restore path in the
      dispatch asm jumps straight to SignalContextRestore, past the
      BOX_PENDSV_RESTORE hook that maintains the per-task box state - so a
      signal-delivered task would resume with g_curBoxId, the MPU box regions
      (R3/R4), g_boxLocalPool and CONTROL/g_sysMode all still describing the
      PREVIOUS task. That is a silent isolation break rather than a crash: the
      task runs its own code under another box's memory map, and no fault
      reports it. Supporting signals under BOX needs that path to re-establish
      box state first; until then the combination is rejected here rather than
      left to fail quietly. The los_box_dispatch.h #error is the backstop for
      configs that bypass Kconfig.
